{{also|-ický|-ičký}}
==English==

===Etymology===
1935, [[American English]]; from ''[[icky-boo]]'' (circa 1920): [[sickly]], [[nauseated]]; [[baby talk]] corruption of '''[[sick]]'''; from a sentimental term for [[Jazz]] music.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɪki/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-icky.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪki|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} [[unpleasantly|Unpleasantly]] [[sticky]]; [[yucky]]; [[disgusting]].
#: {{ux|en|I stepped in something '''icky''' and it smells terrible.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[excessively|Excessively]] [[sentimental]].
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[unwell|Unwell]] or [[upset]]; in a bad state of mind or health.
#: {{ux|en|I'm not going to work today. I just feel '''icky'''.}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|ick}}

